# 4. Main menu and navigation

| Option | Current behavior | Availability and retained information |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PLAY | Opens LEVELS, rather than immediately starting a random puzzle | Available on the main menu. An unfinished playable attempt is saved when leaving for level selection. |
| CONTINUE | Restores the one valid unfinished attempt, including its current board and counters | Hidden and non-interactable when no suitable checkpoint exists. It does not resume a won, lost, fully captured, or exhausted board. |
| CUSTOM | Opens GAME SETUP | Remembers mode, size, difficulty, and fruit-menu preferences. It does not itself replace the current attempt until a game is started. |
| HOW TO PLAY | Opens the instructions panel | BACK returns to the menu. |
| SETTINGS | Opens sound and menu-preview preferences | BACK returns to the main menu when entered from the menu. |
| QUIT | Requests application exit | Hidden on Android and iOS. Actual process closure depends on the platform; Editor play is not the same as a packaged application. |

PLAY is not the same action as CONTINUE. Selecting a new numbered level begins a fresh attempt. Selecting the same numbered level as the saved unfinished game opens “This will restart the level. are you sure you want to continue” with CONTINUE and BACK. Here CONTINUE confirms a restart; it is not the main-menu resume action. BACK preserves the unfinished attempt.

Only one unfinished-session checkpoint is supported. Starting another level can replace the resumable attempt; there is no list of several suspended games. The special restart confirmation applies to the saved same mode/difficulty/level identity. There is no equivalent general warning for every different-level or custom-game replacement.

During gameplay, HOME opens “Are you sure you want to quit to home?” with CONFIRM and BACK. Confirming returns to the menu and saves a still-playable attempt. Cancelling from gameplay resumes it; cancelling a confirmation opened from Pause returns to the paused screen. Pause's MAIN MENU route uses the same confirmation. The level-selection Home action returns directly to the menu; the level-selection screen has no Pause button.

