# 6. Difficulty system

The numbered-level screen uses EASY, MEDIUM, HARD, and EXPERT. Custom setup uses EASY, NORMAL, HARD, and PERFECT. MEDIUM and NORMAL select the same allowance tier; EXPERT and PERFECT select the same strict tier. This naming difference is currently visible to players.

Difficulty does **not** directly change the numbered dimension band, the six available colors, color-clustering probabilities, or the scene's geometry-growth parameters. It changes the selected move allowance and optional-goal tuning. It also participates in the seed identity, so a fresh Easy board and a fresh Expert board at the same level number normally have different color arrangements and may have different irregular geometry. This is seed variation, not proof of a special Expert shape-complexity rule.

| Numbered name | Custom name | Move allowance relative to verified solution | Capture-goal fraction | Efficiency-goal spare-move fraction | Early-goal fraction of solution length | Estimated human seconds per move |
| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| EASY | EASY | Largest extra allowance | 0.45 | 0.65 | 0.35 | 10 |
| MEDIUM | NORMAL | Intermediate extra allowance | 0.65 | 0.50 | 0.30 | 7 |
| HARD | HARD | Small extra allowance | 0.80 | 0.20 | 0.25 | 6 |
| EXPERT | PERFECT | Exactly the retained verified solution length | 0.95 | 0 | 0.20 | 5 |

A fraction of 0.45 for a capture goal does not mean “capture 45% of the whole board.” It scales a demonstrated move's capture result. Exact formulas are in Chapters 13 and 17.

All categories have 100 levels and the same dimension schedule. A later Easy level can therefore be physically larger than an early Expert level. Larger size and more initial connected color regions generally increase planning effort, but no strict monotonic guarantee says Level 40 needs more moves than Level 39. The solver-derived allowance depends on the actual arrangement.

Expert's zero-spare allowance is based on a verified best-known solution, not automatically a mathematically shortest one. If a shorter route is discovered later, the original saved allowance does not automatically shrink. Gold-star thresholds remain the same for every difficulty; this creates an important Expert rating limitation discussed in Chapter 19.

