# 37. Frequently asked questions

**How do I win?** Make all playable cubes one connected color within the allowance. Completing on the last move wins.

**How do colors connect?** Matching cubes must share faces through a chain. Corners, diagonal contacts, and empty space do not count.

**Can I choose any cube?** Yes, any cube that can be reached by the click/tap view, provided its color differs from the selected paint. The game is not restricted to the initial corner region.

**Why did capture progress go down?** You worked on a different component. The bar describes the current component, not all cubes ever visited.

**Does choosing paint spend a move?** No. A legal cube recolor does. Choosing a limited-use goal's named paint can still count as a palette selection even before it is applied.

**Can a move with no added neighbors cost a move?** Yes. Changing a component's color is legal even without a merge.

**Why do same-sized levels have different allowances?** Their colors/regions and verified solutions differ. Allowances use solution length and region complexity.

**Are all numbered levels solvable?** A newly published numbered definition requires a validated within-budget witness. That proves a route, not optimality or freedom from every device/save/runtime failure. Custom emergency allowance is a different recovery case.

**Does the solver always find the shortest route?** No. Only results with a proof are optimal. A bounded validated search normally means best known within the available effort.

**Why might the developer solver fail an Expert level?** Its current plan may be longer than the preserved allowance. A different validated route can exist in the saved definition.

**Why do larger levels take longer to load?** More geometry and regions increase preparation/search work. First-time goal/definition creation also takes time; replay can use a saved definition.

**What distinguishes the modes?** Full Grid is a cube shell; Random Shape is an irregular connected external skin; Items is one of four fruit skins. All share the flood rules and palette.

**What changes with difficulty?** Allowance, goal tuning/pools and the identity seed. Numbered dimensions and palette count do not directly change with difficulty.

**What is my score based on?** A random integer 21–49 times a capture-size band multiplier. It has no time, difficulty or win bonus.

**How do I earn three stars?** Win in no more than 70% of the allowance. The 90% threshold separates two stars from one.

**Can every Expert level earn three stars?** Not necessarily. If its exact-budget witness is a proven minimum, this rating rule allows only one star. That is a current design limitation.

**Are goals mandatory?** No. You can win and unlock the next level without achieving any.

**Can goals be earned across attempts?** Yes, across successful attempts on the same saved numbered definition.

**What if I meet a goal and lose?** It is not newly banked. Previously earned goals remain.

**Does replay generate a different numbered board?** Valid saved definitions restore their exact initial board, allowance and goals. Custom restart is not covered by that guarantee.

**Can a worse replay remove stars?** No. The popup shows that attempt's rating; the tile keeps the maximum saved stars.

**How do I unlock another category?** Every category has Level 1 available; later levels unlock within that category after the preceding win. Success elsewhere does not cross-unlock them.

**Why does the music intensify?** Remaining moves cross 50% or five moves, with the five-move rule taking priority.

**Does Pause freeze everything?** No. It stops gameplay interaction and the active-play clock; existing animation and music can continue. App suspension is handled differently.

**Where are my coins and gems?** The +100/+5 cards are placeholders. No functioning wallet or currency economy is implemented.

**Why is custom fruit play unavailable?** FRUITS is explicitly COMING SOON. The four numbered Items silhouettes are a separate completed route.

**Does it need the internet?** The inspected active puzzle and save systems operate locally. No game account/cloud requirement was found.

**Is progress saved automatically?** Relevant interactions and lifecycle events request local saves. Abrupt termination/storage failure can still lose the latest unsaved change; there is no cloud recovery guarantee.

**Why is Continue missing?** There is no supported, incomplete, restorable checkpoint with remaining moves, or restoration has failed its validity checks.

**Where are the liquid particles?** The optional wave-splash system has been removed. The original color/scale wave remains; victory confetti and UI sparkles are independent.

