# 40. Glossary

| Term | Meaning in this game |
| --- | --- |
| Voxel / cube | One playable cube occupying a grid position |
| Envelope | The possible cubic volume in which an object is constructed |
| Shell / skin | The playable exterior cubes rather than all hidden interior material |
| Face adjacency | Two cube positions differ by one step along exactly one axis |
| Region | A face-connected group of the same color |
| Active component | The connected region at the most recently recolored cube, used for capture tracking |
| Free-region flood | Rules allowing the player to recolor any chosen region, not only one fixed origin |
| Newly captured | In the current component but not in the immediately previous component |
| Palette | The six selectable paint colors |
| Move allowance / budget | Maximum accepted recolors before failure if the board is still incomplete |
| Seed | A reproducible input for geometry/color generation |
| Preserved definition | Saved initial numbered puzzle, palette, allowance, goals and verified route |
| Checkpoint / session | One saved unfinished attempt with changed colors and counters |
| Catalog | Permanent completion/record history for the 1,200 numbered identities |
| Witness | A complete sequence demonstrated to win under the flood rules |
| Validated | That route was replay-checked successfully |
| Best known | Shortest validated route found by the search so far |
| Optimal | No shorter route exists, established by proof rather than hope |
| Heuristic | A useful estimate/ranking that can guide search without guaranteeing the best answer |
| Greedy search | Repeatedly take a promising immediate choice |
| Beam search | Keep a limited collection of promising partial routes |
| Lookahead | Compare a few future moves before deciding |
| IDA* | Repeated bounded-depth search using a safe lower bound to seek shorter solutions |
| Gold stars | Current/best move-efficiency rating, one through three on a win |
| Goal diamond | An optional challenge earned permanently on a qualifying numbered win |
| Active-play time | Time when the attempt is actually interactive, excluding loading/pause/results |
| Solver time | Developer session wall time, which can include analysis and pauses |
| Crossfade | Fade between two music tracks without an abrupt switch |
| Fallback | A recovery route when the preferred generation/search process fails |

