# 41. Completeness audit and verification record

A second review cross-checked the initial description against current saved configuration and edge cases before this document was finalized. In particular:

- The startup build uses the 3D game; the older 2D scene is disabled.
- Numbered mode/difficulty/page identities were compared against actual selection controls and their runtime behavior.
- Difficulty names were checked in authored screens, not inferred from internal terminology.
- The current camera overrides were compared with both defaults and older performance prose; the discrepancy is disclosed.
- Score award bands, random endpoints, same-color invalid moves, free-region capture switching, final-move victory order and rapid-input handling were traced through the active play path.
- Allowance percentages, two-stage rounding, complexity thresholds and strict tier-order guards were checked against the saved Level 1 profile.
- All ten goal types, their twelve weighted pools, family exclusions, witness validation, time-estimate limitation and win-only persistence were reviewed.
- Star thresholds and the different present-win versus best-tile displays were checked independently from diamonds and placeholder currency.
- Actual saved initial Level 1 cells were decoded read-only. Its region identities and the 14-step witness were reconstructed, reproducing 152/152 completion. Goal targets and the illustrative scoring table were recalculated.
- Menu, Continue, pause Settings, Home and same-level restart confirmation routes were compared with their available authored controls.
- Audio clip assignments were separated from actual automatic triggers; dynamic-music priorities, muting and lifecycle saves were reviewed.
- Removed wave-particle functionality was excluded from active features, while independent victory confetti/glow/sparkles were retained.
- Editor-only automation/history and release/development FPS behavior were separated from ordinary player features.
- Current record structures were inspected before making claims about best scores, best times, cloud transfer or rewards.

This is a functionality audit, not a script-by-script reference manual. No existing gameplay, configuration, UI, material, scene, prefab or save was deliberately modified. The only intended new project deliverable is this document. Reading saved data for an example did not replay that attempt in the live application or change its records.

