# 42. Unverified behavior and client acceptance boundaries

The current implementation provides a clear set of testable product behaviors, but this document should not be used as a blanket release sign-off. The following remain outside what this read-only audit freshly established:

| Area | What is established | What remains to verify in a product build |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Core rules and calculations | Inspected rules, exact saved example and recalculated tables | Broad device/end-to-end coverage for all 1,200 identities |
| Mobile input | Touch gestures and UI blocking are implemented | Device-specific sensitivity, accessibility, conflicting gestures and orientation changes |
| Performance | Pooling, bounded search, cooperative preparation and surface-only geometry are implemented | Signed Android/iOS frame time, memory, heat, battery and cold loading |
| Audio | Current assignments, gains, transitions and missing triggers are identified | Perceived loudness, speaker/headphone balance and platform interruptions |
| Persistence | Local checkpoint, immutable definition and catalog validation are implemented | Disk-full, abrupt kill, power-loss and migration/recovery behavior under real platform conditions |
| Content reproducibility | Local saved replay is fixed and witnesses are preserved | Identical first-generation allowances/goals across different device search timing |
| Future updates | Version rejection/preservation protects against silent overwrite | Successful migration of old saves into unimplemented future formats |
| Commercial features | No integrated wallet/shop/cloud requirement found | No claim of an economy, store or online service readiness is made |

For client demonstrations, use the exact names and caveats in this document. In particular, present +100/+5 as placeholders, FRUITS as unavailable custom content, diamonds as goal achievements, and validated as different from optimal. Those distinctions prevent a demonstration of the current game from accidentally promising unfinished functionality.

